  "claims": {
    "scope": "every outcome in this report was measured at the association level (code -> label) on the canonical prompt only, under strict parsing (multi-label = invalid, never first-match), with held-out members ABSENT from the edit's training data; dataset celeba_numeric, 6/6 set-seed cells evaluated, EXECUTED edit seeds [17, 42, 123] (the frozen manifest declares [17, 42, 123]); soft candidate scores are recorded beside every strict decision and never override it",
    "headline": "rule generalization vs entity-specific abstraction (celeba_numeric): across 6 evaluated set-seed cells the strict verdicts are [entity_specific_abstraction=4, indeterminate_members_present=2].  A cell is entity_specific_abstraction only when the edit succeeded on its trained member AND every held-out member kept its own baseline label (boundary-outside members keeping their label count as rule_consistent_boundary_respected); it is rule_generalization only when the edit succeeded AND every held-out branch/interior member followed the rule AND no boundary-outside member crossed into the bin; mixed compositions are reported as mixed_partial_generalization and never collapsed into either pure label; a failed edit is edit_failure_precondition and measures no generalization",
    "not_claimed": [
      "no threshold, gate, promotion criterion or training recipe in this repository changes as a result of this probe, and nothing reads its output",
      "entity_specific here means the held-out member kept its baseline label under THIS edit recipe on the canonical prompt; it is not evidence that no recipe or prompt would generalize -- prompt robustness is the prompt panel's question",
      "rule_generalization here is a behavioral observation about withheld branch members; it is not a claim that the rule is represented symbolically or would transfer beyond the evaluated members",
      "the numeric extension profiles (GRN_24..GRN_29) exist only in this tree; the frozen 24-profile granularity benchmark, its baseline route and its cells are untouched",
      "boundary_outside members keeping their own label are counted as rule_consistent, never as entity_specific: the two outcomes answer different questions and are reported separately everywhere"
